 "description": "Audit a mixed batch of events, each against the schema for its own type. Reports the failing event index, type and pointer for every breach, events carrying no usable type, and event types with no schema supplied - because silently not validating a new type is how it reaches a consumer unchecked. Declared types nothing in the batch used are listed too. Pay 120000 atomic USDC on Base via exact x402. MCP does not pay; it provides a challenge handoff.",
 "inputSchema": {
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {
   "allow_unknown_types": {
    "description": "Treat an event type with no schema as acceptable. Defaults to false; when set, such events are reported as not examined rather than as findings.",
    "type": "boolean"
   },
   "events": {
    "description": "A batch of records as JSON objects, at most 2000. Nothing is fetched, delivered or acknowledged, and no signature or secret is handled.",
    "example": [
     {
      "event_id": "evt-1",
      "offset": 101,
      "order_id": "o-1",
      "schema_version": "2",
      "stream": "orders-0",
      "total": 42.5,
      "type": "order.created"
     },
